WEBVTT

00:12.970 --> 00:18.710
Hikari ga sasu sora, umareochiru kage
In the bright sky illuminated by
sunlight, darkened shadows are born.

00:18.810 --> 00:24.150
Unmei wa dokomademo hikisakareru
Fate itself is being torn apart.

00:25.190 --> 00:30.150
Donna toki mo kesshite akiramenainara
If you never give up, no matter what happens,

00:30.330 --> 00:37.560
mada tozasareteru tobira kanarazu hiraku
Even that locked door will open for you.

00:38.530 --> 00:43.990
Eien datte dakishimete, fuuin mo tokihanachi
Embrace eternity and release the seal.

00:44.070 --> 00:49.940
Mamorubekimono ga ima kokoni wa arukara
Because the ones you wish
to protect are right here.

00:49.940 --> 00:55.880
Namida mo gyutto dakishimete,
yasashisa de tsutsumikomi
Embrace their tears with kindness.

00:55.880 --> 01:01.560
Nagareru mizu no youni tsuyoku nare
Become strong like the formless water,

01:01.560 --> 01:07.550
omouyouni tsuyoku nare
Become as strong as you wish to be.

01:07.700 --> 01:13.170
Mou jibun ni obienaide
Stop being afraid of yourself.

01:13.170 --> 01:19.800
Sou mirai wo osorenaide
Do not fear the future.

01:32.150 --> 01:33.450
I'm home!

01:35.560 --> 01:38.250
Hi, Dad. Mind if we keep a yokai?

01:39.830 --> 01:41.090
A what?

01:49.640 --> 01:51.640
Sure, I guess.

01:51.640 --> 01:53.000
Really?!

01:54.680 --> 01:58.450
As expected from the man chosen
by Miyako. You're very smart!

01:58.450 --> 02:02.580
Just don't talk in front of other people.
It'll cause a commotion.

02:04.720 --> 02:09.660
Our Fox Deity, Takes up Residence

02:16.870 --> 02:19.230
So this is Miyako-sama.

02:21.740 --> 02:25.670
The one next to her is my brother.
He was really small back then.

02:38.550 --> 02:44.250
Is this one on the side the
great mouse of Mt. Kokuten?

02:47.300 --> 02:50.330
Hey. You better make some for me, too.

02:50.330 --> 02:52.230
Okay, but make sure you eat all of it.

02:53.300 --> 02:55.930
Depends how good of a cook you are.

02:56.300 --> 02:59.070
Ko-chan is the Mamorime of the Mizuchi.

02:59.310 --> 03:00.210
A Mamorime?

03:00.540 --> 03:06.920
I have come to protect the master of the Mizuchi
family, Noboru-sama, as well as Toru-sama.

03:06.920 --> 03:10.620
I hope your family knows you're staying here.

03:10.620 --> 03:13.820
I have come under direct
commands of the main family.

03:13.820 --> 03:19.730
Oh, okay. It's rare to see someone so busy at
your age. How long are you going to stay?

03:19.830 --> 03:22.520
Until the day that I die.

03:22.860 --> 03:26.860
Oh. I guess it's going to be a while.

03:27.100 --> 03:31.410
In that case, I better furnish a room for you.

03:31.410 --> 03:36.340
Please pay me no heed.
The yard will suffice.

03:37.380 --> 03:39.380
You enjoy the great outdoors, huh?

03:39.380 --> 03:44.050
The neighbors might call the cops if they
find a young girl sleeping in my yard.

03:44.050 --> 03:46.850
I really prefer you sleep indoors.

03:46.850 --> 03:48.880
I am grateful.

03:53.330 --> 03:56.230
Dinner's ready. You can sit here.

03:58.630 --> 04:01.540
Is this meal for me?

04:01.540 --> 04:02.800
Yeah.

04:02.800 --> 04:06.210
Oh, I'm sorry. You don't like omelets with rice?

04:06.810 --> 04:07.570
It's not that.

04:07.740 --> 04:09.440
Then come over here.

04:09.810 --> 04:10.680
Yes.

04:11.150 --> 04:12.700
Let's eat!

04:19.390 --> 04:21.860
Ko-chan. Do you have any foods you don't like?

04:22.560 --> 04:25.530
There is nothing I dislike
to the point I cannot eat it.

04:26.160 --> 04:29.130
However, centipedes are not my preference.

04:29.360 --> 04:31.000
You've eaten them before?

04:31.000 --> 04:31.870
Yes.

04:31.870 --> 04:33.860
Wow, that's amazing.

04:34.140 --> 04:35.900
I think that's more...

04:37.110 --> 04:38.770
What's that box?

04:39.970 --> 04:43.310
The weather tomorrow will
be sunny and partly cloudy.

04:43.410 --> 04:44.680
The high pressure system will pass
through the north, and by nightfall...

04:44.680 --> 04:46.810
The high pressure system will pass
through the north, and by nightfall...
There's a human inside the box!

04:46.810 --> 04:47.150
The high pressure system will pass
through the north, and by nightfall...

04:47.150 --> 04:47.180
...a low pressure system will
build up off the eastern coast.

04:47.180 --> 04:48.450
...a low pressure system will
build up off the eastern coast.
It's called a TV.

04:48.450 --> 04:48.680
...a low pressure system will
build up off the eastern coast.

04:48.680 --> 04:51.150
...a low pressure system will
build up off the eastern coast.
Who are you?! Are you a yokai?! Answer me!

04:51.150 --> 04:52.850
Who are you?! Are you a yokai?! Answer me!

04:52.920 --> 04:56.760
It's like reviving a caveman in the present day.

04:56.760 --> 04:59.960
That person isn't exactly in the box.

05:04.470 --> 05:05.960
This is pretty interesting.

05:10.370 --> 05:11.670
I remember this.

05:11.740 --> 05:16.840
It's a horror movie where people
die after seeing some cursed video.

05:16.840 --> 05:18.180
It's pretty scary.

05:25.320 --> 05:27.390
Hey, mind if I go to the convenience store?

05:27.390 --> 05:29.860
Go ahead. What're you buying?

05:29.860 --> 05:31.880
A new game's coming out!

05:34.830 --> 05:36.160
Welcome.

05:36.360 --> 05:38.270
I'm going to read some magazines.

05:38.270 --> 05:38.790
Okay.

05:39.530 --> 05:41.970
I'd like to preorder a video game.

05:42.100 --> 05:44.870
Uh... One moment, please.

05:46.040 --> 05:49.140
Did I forget to teach you how to reserve games?

05:49.140 --> 05:49.940
Yes, sir.

05:51.280 --> 05:52.540
Here's the order form.

05:52.750 --> 05:55.550
It's always in here, so remember that, okay?

05:55.550 --> 05:56.180
Yes, sir.

05:56.720 --> 05:57.690
Now then...

05:58.320 --> 06:03.060
Can you write your name and
phone number in the box?

06:03.060 --> 06:04.420
Sure.

06:08.800 --> 06:10.790
The thing on your wrist looks neat.

06:18.140 --> 06:19.400
Where are you going?

06:19.640 --> 06:23.300
I'm going out with Handa and Kubota.
We're on spring break, you know?

06:23.440 --> 06:24.670
Who're they?

06:26.150 --> 06:27.050
My friends.

06:27.150 --> 06:29.780
Oh. Hold on for just a second.

06:29.780 --> 06:30.580
Okay.

06:38.330 --> 06:40.850
Ku-chan, do you even know what that is?

06:41.260 --> 06:42.420
Of course I do.

06:49.240 --> 06:50.730
What are you doing?

06:53.270 --> 06:54.070
Here.

06:55.380 --> 06:57.400
My scent's on it.

06:59.980 --> 07:01.920
Humans can't smell it.

07:02.350 --> 07:06.510
Be sure to wear it any time you plan to go out.

07:06.920 --> 07:08.950
It should protect you from a lot of things.

07:11.960 --> 07:13.550
That's a kumihimo braid.

07:13.690 --> 07:16.490
You have really nice taste. Where did you buy it?

07:16.900 --> 07:17.870
It was a gift.

07:18.370 --> 07:19.260
Oh, really.

07:20.770 --> 07:21.830
Here.

07:23.100 --> 07:27.470
The game will arrive on the 11th of next
month. Please come pick it up then.

07:28.780 --> 07:30.510
Thank you very much!

07:33.380 --> 07:36.420
You know that guy's the store owner?

07:36.420 --> 07:38.780
You mean the brown-haired guy? No way!

07:39.120 --> 07:44.150
Yeah way. I saw some other clerk
call him "Owner" the other day.

07:44.290 --> 07:46.690
He looks so young and he's already
a store owner? That's impressive.

07:46.690 --> 07:48.090
Yeah, really.

07:51.870 --> 07:54.270
Is there anything I can help with?

07:56.200 --> 07:59.640
Can you go hang the laundry, then?

08:00.070 --> 08:01.700
It should all still be in the washing machine.

08:02.210 --> 08:03.440
Right away.

08:07.720 --> 08:09.910
I guess I should make lunch soon.

08:14.190 --> 08:15.380
Who's there?!

08:16.720 --> 08:17.660
It's cold!

08:19.030 --> 08:20.050
Ku?!

08:21.060 --> 08:22.960
I'm going to sleep here all summer.

08:22.960 --> 08:27.130
Don't leave it open. You're wasting electricity.

08:27.130 --> 08:29.640
Wait, why'd you switch to your male form?

08:29.640 --> 08:31.540
I thought you were a woman earlier.

08:31.540 --> 08:32.740
No real reason.

08:32.740 --> 08:35.110
Uh huh. So where's Toru?

08:35.110 --> 08:40.170
He went out with two people called Handa
and Kubota. Something about spring break.

08:40.520 --> 08:41.880
You sure you didn't need to go with him?

08:42.650 --> 08:44.140
I got it covered.

08:44.920 --> 08:49.120
Besides, Toru would feel uncomfortable
if I followed him everywhere.

08:49.260 --> 08:51.130
I guess so.

08:51.130 --> 08:53.830
Besides, it'd be a pain in the ass for me, too.

08:53.830 --> 08:54.560
Hey!

08:54.560 --> 08:55.820
I'm home!

09:03.770 --> 09:04.640
Ko-san?

09:05.470 --> 09:07.130
Please, just call me Ko.

09:07.540 --> 09:09.410
Oh, okay.

09:09.410 --> 09:11.910
Anyway, Ko. Lunch is ready.

09:11.910 --> 09:12.680
Understood.

09:16.250 --> 09:19.520
What's the biggest shrine around here?

09:19.520 --> 09:22.220
The Hashiba Shrine, I think.

09:22.490 --> 09:24.130
I need to go pay a visit.

09:24.130 --> 09:25.060
To who?

09:25.060 --> 09:26.890
The deity of this land.

09:26.890 --> 09:27.520
Who's that?

09:27.760 --> 09:31.970
Each land has a deity governing it.

09:31.970 --> 09:37.870
Anyone born in another land who wants
to use their powers in the new land...

09:37.870 --> 09:42.710
...must pay a visit to the presiding
deity and receive their blessing.

09:44.910 --> 09:47.240
What does the shrine worship?

09:47.520 --> 09:48.570
Beats me.

09:48.950 --> 09:50.940
Why don't you know?

09:51.420 --> 09:53.610
I don't think anyone around here knows.

09:55.160 --> 09:56.820
That's pitiful.

09:58.530 --> 09:59.620
Take me there.

10:05.430 --> 10:06.800
Farewell.

10:07.440 --> 10:08.770
You're not coming with us, Ko?

10:09.140 --> 10:11.910
I still have some laundry to hang.

10:11.910 --> 10:13.030
You can do that later.

10:13.310 --> 10:17.110
No. I must fulfill the orders given unto me.

10:17.410 --> 10:18.970
Even at the cost of my life.

10:21.450 --> 10:22.680
Oh, okay.

10:25.790 --> 10:27.550
I hope it won't rain.

10:27.820 --> 10:30.420
Especially after all the trouble Ko is
going through to hang the laundry.

10:31.760 --> 10:38.600
That Mamorime is quick with her spells, but
she's so clumsy when it comes to anything else.

10:45.340 --> 10:47.100
Why, hello.

10:47.540 --> 10:48.200
Hello.

10:49.780 --> 10:54.180
Are you the elder brother? Your younger
brother is a frequent patron at my store.

10:54.180 --> 10:55.710
Oh, hi.

10:56.680 --> 11:00.420
But you don't get to see a fox
hanging out with humans everyday...

11:19.710 --> 11:20.830
Who are you?

11:20.910 --> 11:25.370
You come into my land and
that's how you talk to me?

11:25.510 --> 11:26.810
Why don't you name yourself first?

11:29.850 --> 11:31.410
I am the tenko Kugen.

11:32.320 --> 11:35.720
Kugen? The Kugen Fox of Mizuchi.

11:35.720 --> 11:40.160
You're that great astral fox.
It's an honor to meet you.

11:40.430 --> 11:45.090
But I heard Kugen was sealed
by the Mizuchi shaman.

11:45.530 --> 11:46.700
I was released.

11:46.700 --> 11:50.600
Now I'm the guardian deity
of the Takagami brothers.

11:51.010 --> 11:56.000
I'll be residing in this land for a while.
I hope you'll make the proper arrangements.

11:56.180 --> 12:02.780
Hello to you, too. My name is Ebisu.
I'm the god governing over the lands around here.

12:03.250 --> 12:05.120
I'm also the owner of this convenience store.

12:05.120 --> 12:05.390
Ebisu

12:05.390 --> 12:06.890
Ebisu
Nice to meet ya.

12:06.890 --> 12:07.110
Ebisu

12:08.120 --> 12:09.150
He's even not hiding it.

12:09.960 --> 12:11.750
Come along to my shrine.

12:12.130 --> 12:12.680
Very well.

12:15.760 --> 12:19.530
Why is the local deity running a convenience store?

12:19.870 --> 12:24.900
With the bad economy and everything,
the donations at my shrine aren't enough.

12:25.240 --> 12:26.710
Is that how it is?

12:26.810 --> 12:31.270
Of course. Money makes the
world go 'round. Every world.

12:33.110 --> 12:37.780
I'm a god of flourishing business.
That's why I started up my own store.

12:38.250 --> 12:45.230
I thought since a god of business
is in the store, I can profit from it.

12:45.230 --> 12:48.680
I didn't know that kind of stuff worked on yourself.

12:50.000 --> 12:52.490
Of course it does.

12:55.400 --> 12:58.000
It's been so long since I last came here.

13:05.750 --> 13:08.610
Let me introduce you to my great underlings.

13:11.390 --> 13:12.880
Koga, Eiga!

13:37.580 --> 13:39.680
The komainu are nothing but guard dogs.

13:39.680 --> 13:43.980
As long as Ebisu doesn't order them,
they won't hurt you.

13:45.090 --> 13:46.290
Oh.

13:46.290 --> 13:49.810
Sorry about that. Did I scare you?

13:51.690 --> 13:55.330
Koga and Eiga. These people are...

13:55.330 --> 13:58.460
...intruders who intend to bring ruin to this land.

14:00.130 --> 14:01.640
Destroy them at once.

14:01.640 --> 14:02.730
Understood.

14:04.610 --> 14:06.300
What did you say, Ebisu?

14:13.350 --> 14:15.150
I don't know why you're doing this...

14:15.150 --> 14:18.180
But if it's a fight you're looking for, you got it.

14:19.650 --> 14:21.180
You two, stay here.

14:25.960 --> 14:27.930
Why are you doing this?!

14:27.930 --> 14:29.450
You call yourself a god?!

14:30.060 --> 14:32.090
We only came here to say hi!

14:33.230 --> 14:36.260
We grown-ups have complicated
circumstances to consider, kid.

14:36.800 --> 14:40.570
Anyway, let's sit back and watch.

14:41.340 --> 14:45.440
You don't get to see the
great tenko fight every day.

15:05.700 --> 15:07.760
Don't glare at me like that.

15:08.340 --> 15:12.540
What have I done to anger you so?

15:12.540 --> 15:13.630
Fool.

15:13.840 --> 15:16.310
You cannot seduce us.

15:17.140 --> 15:21.810
I wanted to end this peacefully,
but you want to take it the hard way.

15:22.620 --> 15:25.880
If you want to get hurt that badly,
I'll be happy to help!

15:30.420 --> 15:31.760
This is annoying!

15:49.540 --> 15:53.740
I thought furry, four-legged
beasts would be weak to fire.

15:54.150 --> 15:57.550
The same applies to you, fox!

16:07.900 --> 16:08.550
Ku-chan!

16:14.770 --> 16:15.740
Bastards!

16:21.040 --> 16:22.530
Shoo! Shoo!

16:22.840 --> 16:23.430
Toru?!

16:24.080 --> 16:25.410
Shoo! Shoo!

16:26.110 --> 16:28.050
Shoo! Shoo!

16:34.420 --> 16:35.390
Stay away from me!

16:35.660 --> 16:36.320
Yeah.

16:39.130 --> 16:40.680
Got your shadow!

16:43.330 --> 16:44.130
What did you do to us?!

16:44.470 --> 16:47.070
It's my ninja spell, Shadow Bind.

16:47.070 --> 16:49.630
Well? You can't move, can you?

16:51.370 --> 16:52.930
How do you like that?

16:53.110 --> 16:54.140
- Move your leg.

16:54.140 --> 16:54.570
- Oh?
- Move your leg.

16:54.780 --> 16:55.840
Ko-chan!

16:55.840 --> 16:58.970
You got some nerve, ordering around the local god.

16:59.850 --> 17:03.910
I don't care who you are.
I won't allow anyone to cast a spell on them.

17:04.180 --> 17:06.150
You're the Mamorime of the Mizuchi...

17:06.550 --> 17:10.850
You know, I did this spell for their safety.

17:13.230 --> 17:14.560
Thanks, Ko.

17:14.800 --> 17:17.490
Yes. I finished hanging all the laundry.

17:18.130 --> 17:19.430
That's not what I meant.

17:23.640 --> 17:27.330
Tenko-sama, the komainu
are not of the metal affinity.

17:28.010 --> 17:32.670
They were carved from a single stone
and given life by the god, Ebisu.

17:33.210 --> 17:35.910
They are incarnations of stone,
yokai of the earth affinity!

17:36.320 --> 17:39.880
If they're made of earth,
of course they'd be resistant to fire.

17:48.960 --> 17:51.330
Wood parts the earth.

17:53.530 --> 17:55.300
These clouds should be enough...

17:55.300 --> 17:57.240
...to find that!

17:57.240 --> 18:02.540
Primordial Heaven-4, Primordial Heaven-2,
Manifested Heaven-3!

18:04.140 --> 18:04.970
Come this way.

18:10.050 --> 18:12.380
What is Ku-chan trying to do?

18:12.720 --> 18:16.420
I believe that it is summoning the Shin.

18:16.790 --> 18:17.690
The Shin?

18:45.650 --> 18:48.120
So what was the point of all this?

18:49.490 --> 18:51.550
You sure broke this place up real nicely.

18:54.230 --> 18:59.390
A god can't destroy his own shrine, you know.

19:00.170 --> 19:01.230
Uh, what?

19:02.170 --> 19:03.840
For the next few days or weeks...

19:03.840 --> 19:09.540
...there will be lots of construction workers
and landscapers coming here non-stop.

19:09.540 --> 19:11.070
When that happens...

19:11.550 --> 19:13.510
...who do you think will benefit the most?

19:13.950 --> 19:17.150
The workers coming here to do the repairs?

19:17.150 --> 19:18.020
That's true.

19:18.390 --> 19:23.790
But the one receiving the biggest
boost is the nearby convenience store.

19:24.290 --> 19:27.920
They'll come to buy drinks
and lunchboxes and stuff!

19:28.730 --> 19:29.530
Excuse me?

19:29.900 --> 19:33.960
Plus, my local parishioners will
be footing the bill for the repairs.

19:34.540 --> 19:36.830
So I don't need to pay a thing.

19:37.270 --> 19:39.210
So you caused all this trouble...

19:39.210 --> 19:42.180
...just to sell more stuff at your store?

19:42.180 --> 19:43.110
Yep.

19:48.620 --> 19:51.780
I don't get how he thinks.

19:51.890 --> 19:52.480
Me neither.

19:53.090 --> 19:57.020
Hey! He never gave me his words of blessing!

19:59.060 --> 20:00.360
Go on home without me!

20:23.520 --> 20:26.040
Both you and the Mamorime will reside here...

20:26.750 --> 20:30.820
That means the Takagami brothers are
descendants of the water priestess.

20:30.820 --> 20:33.350
You got a problem with that?

20:33.690 --> 20:35.060
No, not really.

20:35.700 --> 20:41.660
That makes their late mother
the water priestess of Mizuchi.

20:42.000 --> 20:43.800
Hmm... I see it now.

20:44.300 --> 20:46.140
You know Miyako?

20:46.140 --> 20:47.830
I never met her in person...

20:48.540 --> 20:50.010
But I always felt her presence.

20:51.850 --> 20:54.550
Just give me your words of blessing.

20:54.550 --> 20:59.110
I'm really torn on whether or not I should.

20:59.820 --> 21:01.010
Say it.

21:01.520 --> 21:03.320
Here goes.

21:04.120 --> 21:05.830
The soul of Takagami Miyako...

21:05.830 --> 21:08.560
...still wanders these lands.

21:21.640 --> 21:23.370
Good work.

21:24.340 --> 21:28.540
Let's see what that fox will do now.

21:40.430 --> 21:46.890
Sora no hate ga tsunagaru basho wo
Where the horizon meets the earth,

21:47.370 --> 21:54.570
no ni saku hana wa mada kitto shiranai
The flower growing in the wild remains unaware.

21:55.940 --> 22:02.440
Kokoyori ii sekai ga aruto
While thinking that there
is a world better than this.

22:02.580 --> 22:10.220
Kokoro wa itsumo hane wo hirogetagaru
They always desire to spread
the wings of their hearts.

22:11.120 --> 22:18.160
Yume dakede owarasenai
Don't let it end as just a dream,

22:18.770 --> 22:25.260
chansu ga aru hazusa
There's always a chance.

22:25.470 --> 22:32.910
Daijoubu bokura wa hitori janai
It's all right. We are not alone.

22:32.910 --> 22:40.520
Kaze ga nanika wo iouto shiteru
The winds are telling us something.

22:40.520 --> 22:48.200
Daijoubu kanarazu umaku yareru
It's all right. You can do it.

22:48.200 --> 22:59.440
Omoi wa itsuka jibun wo kaeru michi ni naru
Those dreams are a path you'll change yourself.

23:03.440 --> 23:06.210
I want to make a cursed video of my own!

23:25.030 --> 23:25.870
Next Time

23:25.870 --> 23:27.130
Next Time
It's now spring, time for the new school year.

23:27.130 --> 23:30.240
Next Time
It really worries me that I have
to leave Ku and Ko at home...

23:30.240 --> 23:32.710
Next Time
...but I'll get even more
worried if they came to school.

23:32.710 --> 23:33.040
Next Time

23:33.040 --> 23:35.040
Next Time
Next time, "Our Fox Deity, Goes to School."

23:35.040 --> 23:35.180
Next Time
Life is best lived frugally, humbly,
diligently, healthily and peacefully!

23:35.180 --> 23:39.350
Next Time
